---
title: AeroPress Latte Shot
description: Espresso-style AeroPress shot with a metal filter and a 15-second stir, topped with steamed milk.
tags: [coffee]
course: drink
icons: [coffee-beans, aeropress, cow]
difficulty: easy
source:
  name: AeroPress
  url: https://aeropress.com/blogs/aeropress-recipes/an-espresso-style-shot-with-aeropress
adapted: true
servings: 1
time: 3m
---

Put the #metal filter{} in the pressure cap of the #AeroPress{}. Screw the cap on.

Add the @coffee{19%g}(ground at 6 on a Baratza Encore). Shake to level.

Pour in the @water{60%g}(just off the boil).

Stir for ~stir{15%seconds}.

Plunge straight through. Speed up at the end.

Top with the @milk{150-180%g}(steamed).

> **Dialing It In** — Change one thing at a time.

> - Gritty or hard to press: grind at 7.

> - Thin or sour: grind at 5.

> - Want less texture: stop pressing at the hiss.

> **What's Changed** — The steps are AeroPress's official recipe. The grind, water temperature and milk amount are adjustments.
